          "note": "Do: Use a public repository on the free plan, inspect GitHub Desktop Changes for unexpected files or secrets, commit the reviewed source, push normally, configure Pages to deploy from the intended branch and root folder, and open the URL from “Viewing your published site.”\n\nFinished when: The repository contains only reviewed source and safe fixtures, Pages reports a successful deployment, and the HTTPS github.io URL loads the intended site.\n\nAccess: A verified free GitHub account, authenticated GitHub Desktop or browser access, network connection, and a public repository are required. GitHub Pages is publicly visible; no paid plan is required for this public route.\n\nNext: Repeat every path-sensitive matrix row at the live URL and record the deployment URL in the README."
